    challengesLabel: THE CHALLENGES
    challenge: <p data-start="349" data-end="611"><strong data-start="349" data-end="389">Complex quotations and work packages</strong><br data-start="389" data-end="392">Every construction site is unique. Structuring a quotation with detailed work packages — items, materials, labor hours — takes too much time in Excel. And an error in one work package impacts the entire billing process.</p><p data-start="613" data-end="808"><strong data-start="613" data-end="656">Time tracking and profitability by site</strong><br data-start="656" data-end="659">Without a centralized tool, it is impossible to know whether a project is profitable before it is completed. Hours recorded on paper arrive too late.</p><p data-start="810" data-end="1003"><strong data-start="810" data-end="851">Planning and subcontractor management</strong><br data-start="851" data-end="854">Coordinating several subcontractors on the same site, planning interventions, and validating their invoices without losing track is a daily headache.</p><p data-start="1005" data-end="1194"><strong data-start="1005" data-end="1040">Periodic maintenance management</strong><br data-start="1040" data-end="1043">Managing recurring maintenance contracts, planning interventions, and generating the related invoices without spending administrative time every month.</p><p data-start="1196" data-end="1416"><strong data-start="1196" data-end="1216">Billing &amp; PEPPOL</strong><br data-start="1216" data-end="1219">Billing at the right time based on the actual progress of the site, collecting payments on site, and complying with the Belgian 2026 e-invoicing obligation — natively, not with a last-minute patch.</p>
- discriminant: odooExpertise
